p.src:
Even a time-independent field changes along the particle’s path because the particle samples different positions. The total derivative is $\frac{dA_m(x(t),t)}{dt}
=
\partial_0A_m+\dot x^n\partial_nA_m.$ The first term is explicit time dependence; the second is implicit time dependence through $x^n(t)$.

