Define the electric components in the convention of the derivation by $E_m=\partial_0A_m-\partial_mA_0.$ The spatial antisymmetric combination $C_{mn}
\equiv
\partial_nA_m-\partial_mA_n$ contains the three independent components of the curl of the vector potential. Its orientation is chosen so that $\dot x^nC_{mn}
=
\left(\mathbf v\times\mathbf B\right)_m.$ Equation  is therefore the relativistic momentum form of . The factor under the time derivative is the relativistic momentum per unit mass, not the Newtonian velocity alone.

