Both sides now have the transformation character of a four-vector. The three spatial equations are therefore components of $\boxed{
m\frac{d^2x^\mu}{d\tau^2}
=
e\left(\partial_\nu A^\mu-\partial^\mu A_\nu\right)u^\nu
}.$ If one defines $F_{\mu\nu}
\equiv
\partial_\mu A_\nu-\partial_\nu A_\mu,$ then the index order and interaction sign used in this lecture give the equivalent compact form $m\frac{du^\mu}{d\tau}
=
-eF^\mu{}_\nu u^\nu.$

